<title>GERMANY: End-Nov Ivorian cocoa arrivals seen 400,000 T - A&amp;D.</title>
<headline>End-Nov Ivorian cocoa arrivals seen 400,000 T - A&amp;D.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cocoa arrivals in Ivorian export ports by the end of November may be 400,000 tonnes, German trader Albrecht &amp; Dill (A&amp;D) said in a weekly report.</p>
<p>The trader noted 40,000 tonnes had reached ports by the end of October, down from 84,000 tonnes a year ago, when harvesting began earlier.</p>
<p>A&amp;D also noted the 1996/97 season could bring a world cocoa supply deficit, but this could be met by existing global stocks, which were estimated at 900,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
